  <reporting-org ref="GB-CHC-1120413" type="21" xml:lang="EN">MICAIA</reporting-org>
  <title xml:lang="EN">Including the poorest: a new approach to honey trade development in Mozambique</title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">This project will enable at least 500 of the poorest most vulnerable women, including female-headed households, in Manica Province, Mozambique, to participate in commercial beekeeping and earn significant new income and develop skills, knowledge and confidence to sustain their livelihood. The project will educate the public in Manica Province on the benefits of honey as a valuable nutritional supplement and will mobilize unemployed youth to help promote and sell honey in rural areas.</description>
  <participating-org role="IMPLEMENTING" type="22" xml:lang="PT">MICAIA Foundation</participating-org>
  <activity-status code="2" xml:lang="EN">The project is at an advanced stage. 550 women have been mobilized and are formed in groups, each one managing a minimum of 50 top bar hives. Training has been provided. The groups also provide a platform for broader \&apos;capabilities\&apos; discussions and learning opportunities. Support for the beekeeping process has led to rapid colonization by bees with prospect of a good initial harvest. Other project activities under way include design of information on honey for use in public institutions such as clinics; and also training of young people as vendors of natural products.</activity-status>
  <activity-date iso-date="2013-04-01" type="START-PLANNED" xml:lang="EN"></activity-date>
